sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Tech Lead / Repository Admin
    participant DASH as Next.js Dashboard
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    User->>DASH: open Review History
    DASH->>GW: GET /v1/reviews?limit=25&offset=0
    GW->>GW: resolve session, scope every query to the caller's organization
    GW->>DB: select reviews joined to repositories, ordered by created_at desc
    DB-->>GW: rows + total count
    GW-->>DASH: items[] + pageInfo
    DASH-->>User: table of PRs with status chips, finding counts, timestamps (AC-09)

    User->>DASH: filter by repository, status, severity and date
    DASH->>GW: GET /v1/reviews?repositoryId=…&status=partial&minSeverity=critical&from=…
    GW->>DB: same query with the filters applied
    alt no reviews match
        DB-->>GW: 0 rows
        GW-->>DASH: items = [], pageInfo.total = 0
        DASH-->>User: empty state rather than an empty table (UC-5 alternate flow)
    else rows returned
        DB-->>GW: filtered rows
        GW-->>DASH: items[] + pageInfo
        DASH-->>User: filtered list
    end

    User->>DASH: select one pull request
    DASH->>GW: GET /v1/reviews/{reviewId}
    GW->>DB: load review, agent_runs, findings, suggestions, similar issues
    DB-->>GW: combined report rows
    GW-->>DASH: CombinedReport — de-duplicated, ranked by severity then confidence
    DASH-->>User: report detail with critical / warning / auto-fixed counts

    User->>DASH: filter the report to one agent
    DASH->>GW: GET /v1/reviews/{reviewId}?agent=security
    GW-->>DASH: the same report, findings narrowed to that agent (FR-WEB-04)
    DASH-->>User: per-agent view

    Note over DASH,DB: agents that timed out are shown as no result with their<br/>recorded latency, so a partial review explains itself (NFR-12)

    Note over User,DASH: severity colours and wording here match the<br/>GitHub comments and Check Run (NFR-08)
